findings.body:
All the new tests only check that violations are reported. None checks that valid input produces no messages, for example:
- an identical anchor in the translation;
- allowed tags like `<br />` or `<b>` when the English value has HTML;
- entities like `&laquo;`;
- `{{x}}` placeholders.

The verifier's unescape and comment-stripping normalization is fragile. Without negative tests, false positives that break the build would go unnoticed.
